    console.log(relative("reports", "reports/2026"));
} // output: 2026
```

Identical or equivalently resolved paths return an empty string. Parent components describe leaving the starting location; component prefixes such as foo and foobar are distinct. POSIX comparisons are case-sensitive and emit slash. Windows comparisons are case-insensitive and emit backslash; another drive or UNC server can require an absolute destination. Drive-relative inputs use the corresponding drive directory when available. Trailing separators do not remain. Unicode text is preserved without normalization. No path needs to exist; no symlink resolution or containment guarantee is provided. If a required working-directory lookup fails, or that directory cannot be represented as valid UTF-8, throws an Error with code path-relative. Identical inputs and fully qualified paths avoid unnecessary directory lookup. Native strings contain valid UTF-8 text.

Ownership: both inputs are borrowed; the result owns its contents.

