Returns the number of declared positions in a fixed tuple. Takes no arguments. The result is int; the tuple is unchanged and length cannot be assigned. An empty tuple has length zero. Each position keeps its declared type and is accessed with a constant integer index. Out-of-range indices are rejected. Tuple positions may be replaced with values of their declared types; variable-length array mutation methods are unavailable.

```tsrust
